<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">Notes :-  n1. The above statement has been prepared in accordance with the Companies (Indian Accounting  nStandards) Rules, 2015 (Ind-AS) prescribed under Section 133 of the Companies Act, 2013 and  nother recognized accounting practices and policies to the extent applicable.  n2. Revenue for the nine months ended on 31st December, 2017 was reported inclusive of Excise  nDuty (till 30th June, 2017). Excise duty, service tax and other indirect taxes were replaced by  nGoods &amp; Services Tax (GST) w.e.f. 01st July, 2017. Accordingly, as per IND AS, Revenues for  nnine months period ended on 31st December, 2018 and 31st December, 2017 are not  ncomparable.  n3. Effective April 01, 2018, the Company has adopted Ind AS - 115 “Revenue from Contracts with  nCustomers” using the modified retrospective approach and cumulative effect, resulting in  nreduction of Rs, 723 lakhs in the opening balance of retained earnings. Due to the adoption of  nInd AS – 115, current nine months Revenue and Profit before tax is higher by Rs. 2693 lakhs  nand Rs. 723 lakhs respectively and hence the same are not comparable to the previous period  ndisclosed.  n4. The other income of Rs. 229 lakhs for the quarter ended December, 2018 (for September–18  nQtr Rs. 432 lakhs, for December–17 Qtr Rs. 291 lakhs) includes interest charged to  nsubsidiaries of Rs. 236 lakhs for December-18 Qtr (for September–18 Qtr Rs. 163 lakhs, for  nDecember–17 Qtr Rs. 150 lakhs), foreign exchange fluctuation loss of Rs. 67 lakhs for  nDecember-18 Qtr (for September–18 Qtr gain of Rs. 216 lakhs, for December–17 Qtr loss Rs.  n64 lakhs), interest on VAT refund received for December-18 Qtr Rs. Nil (for September–18 Qtr  nRs. 46 lakhs, for December–17 Qtr Rs. Nil), finance income on Financial Guarantee of Rs. 51  nlakhs for December-18 Qtr (for September–18 Qtr Rs. 10 lakhs, for December–17 Qtr Rs. 28  nlakhs), finance income on Redemption of Investment for December-18 Qtr Rs. Nil (for  nSeptember–18 Qtr Rs. Nil, for December–17 Qtr Rs. 160 lakhs) and other Misc. Income of Rs. 9  nlakhs (for September–18 Qtr Rs. -3 lakhs, for December–17 Qtr Rs. 17 lakhs).  n5. The company has only one operating segment viz. Auto Components and accordingly there are  nno separate reportable segments in the context of Ind-AS 108 “Operating Segment”.  n6. The above financial results were reviewed and recommended by the Audit Committee at its  nmeeting held on 11th February, 2019 and subsequently approved by the Board of Directors at  nits meeting held on 11th February, 2019. The Statutory Auditors have carried out a limited  nreview of the financial results for the quarter/nine month period ended 31st December, 2018.  n7. Previous period figures have been regrouped/rearranged wherever considered necessary.  nFor and behalf of the Board  nPlace : Mumbai Harish Sheth  nDate : 11th February, 2019 Chairman &amp; Managing Director  nDIN : 01434459 </in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
